WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:02.035
My next guest, retired U.S.

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.370
Admiral Mike Mullen, spent

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.505
four decades serving his country,

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.140
and then he served as President

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.141
Obama's chairman

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.642
of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.410
And he's joining me

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.512
now live from Annapolis, Maryland.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.680
Admiral Mullen,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.882
welcome back to the program.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.050
So, you know,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.551
the word Bermuda has been on

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.821
everybody's lips for a long, long time.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:25.859
How do you assess it's its nature

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.294
to the prosecution of this war?

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.600
Well, I think it's I basically agree.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:33.900
I don't

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.535
I don't think strategically

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.069
in terms

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.605
of the progress on the ground

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.940
that it's overly significant.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.542
But I do think

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.077
from both sides, actually,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.812
both Ukraine and Russia,

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:49.849
that it it provides it's almost symbolic.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.752
And it's been six or seven months that

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.287
the Ukrainians have

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.922
been fiercely defending

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.191
back Mount

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:58.925
And it's also

00:00:58.925 --> 00:00:59.759
been obviously

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.028
that long that the Russians

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.930
have been attacking it.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.199
And one of the things that

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.569
it's just a fact is because of the effort

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.605
in defense, the Russians have expended

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:16.409
a tremendous amount of resources.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.445
They've lost thousands

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:20.280
and thousands of soldiers,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:20.880
that they've

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.149
lost an enormous amount of equipment.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.186
And so whether tactically,

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.521
it's a huge gain or

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.856
loss on the ground,

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.292
I think in terms of impact of the war,

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.260
it's had a significant impact

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.096
on what Russia can do.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.898
And I think it in its own way,

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.701
starts to limit what they can do

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.002
in other places.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.370
For instance, in the South,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.573
which is a place you just talked about

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.141
So, Admiral Mullen,

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:49.275
you just mentioned something

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.777
that the NATO has just

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.712
just confirmed, at least

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.881
an official of NATO's

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.216
actually talking anonymously

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.152
saying that they believe Russia has lost

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.689
perhaps five times as many forces

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.457
on the ground as Ukraine

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.226
during this battle for Obama.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.060
So, you know,

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.194
you just explained

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.629
what that might mean for

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.297
Russia trying to, you know,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.399
secure itself in the south.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.734
But also, let's just stick

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.935
with Ukraine for a second.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.438
Because you've all described it as

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:21.141
a pretty much kind of a do or die

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.375
and certainly symbolic.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.009
You remember

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.011
President Zelensky went to Obama

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.980
on the eve of his visit to Congress.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.315
He brought back a flag that he said

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.416
a soldier from

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.252
Bermuda gave him to take

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.887
to the United States.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.755
So it's hugely symbolic

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.991
and they've lost a lot of people.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.125
How will that affect

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.294
the mindset of commanders and troops

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.162
if they have to

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:42.896
then turn around

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.397
and launch a counteroffensive

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.098
somewhere else?

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:46.733
Well, I

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:47.634
think knowing

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.301
what they know

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.603
in terms of the progress of the battle

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.271
and it's

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.541
it's a city, I think it's some 70,000

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.042
and reports are now

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.545
there are four or 5000 left.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.913
And also

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:04.050
viewing the the photographs of the rubble

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.152
that black mud has become,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:06.853
which I think is

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.354
what Putin is trying to do

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.255
across the country

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.290
to ruin

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.325
as much of the country as possible.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.993
You know, it will have its effect.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.795
That said,

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.830
those losses that we described

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.631
earlier with the Russians

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.668
are typical of their inability to fight.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:23.703
And I think one of the things

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:24.337
to your point

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.672
about the counteroffensive

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.907
when it comes in the spring,

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:31.878
we will find the Ukrainian military

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.179
much more capable

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:33.813
of what

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.748
we call combined arms

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.785
training, the coordination of air

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.653
artillery, armor.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.056
They will have much more armor

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.824
available to them,

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.526
if you will, and the Bradleys

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.528
and the strikers that are over there.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.129
And so I think in the

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.197
in the long run,

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:54.567
it puts Ukraine in a much better position

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.003
to fight, to continue the fight.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.438
And. And I.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.473
Russia's given me no indication

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.976
that they are capable

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.879
of dramatically changing how they fight

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.115
while they continue to sustain

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.817
sustain these huge losses.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.018
And I think that will be

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:12.885
that will happen

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.288
in the counteroffensive as well.

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.290
So, you know, we again

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.726
heard from the head of the sorry,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.227
the head of the Volga group,

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.862
who is Prigozhin

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.364
who is complaining bitterly,

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.832
along with his forces

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.834
of a lack of ammunition,

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.736
a lack of shells and the like.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.871
But we also know that Ukraine is lacking,

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:32.538
that we know

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.940
that the EU is earmarked

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.541
$1,000,000,000 for one

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.510
55 millimeter artillery shells,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.646
but they haven't got them yet.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.881
And you're talking about this

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.715
spring offensive,

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.417
which to be fair,

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.985
in spring is March 20th.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.154
That's just three weeks away.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:50.056
Do you think they're ready for a four

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.924
an offensive to start that soon?

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.093
Well, I think

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.396
the question is a great question,

00:04:56.396 --> 00:05:00.366
because in a way, Christiane, this fight

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.636
has evolved into a battle of attrition.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.570
And so

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.639
and battles of attrition are oftentimes

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.375
won by that, the health

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.078
or lack thereof of the industrial base.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.146
So clearly,

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.681
both sides are focused

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:17.717
on this potential shortage of ammunition.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:18.751
And it's really critical,

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.653
particularly for the Ukrainians

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.922
to be very selective

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.957
about the use of the munitions

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.025
that they have,

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:28.194
because obviously the supply

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.462
isn't infinite.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.963
But you also hear that,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:31.297
you know,

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.099
Russia's having the same problem.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:35.468
So I think everybody's aware of that

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.770
and the commitments as well as

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.706
creating the production lines,

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.508
which is which can be a problem as well,

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:44.744
which will produce that the munitions

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.879
for the future fight. And I think

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:49.215
everybody would like

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.250
one would like this to end

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.385
you know, immediately.

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:53.786
Secondly, there's discussions

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.555
on how it ends.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:56.923
But my sense, Christiane,

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.891
is this counteroffensive

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:01.361
and the results of that for the rest of

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:03.629
this year will really set the stage

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.564
for when this ends.

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.232
And I actually hope

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.567
that it's sooner

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:08.701
rather than later,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.537
sometime late this year,

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:11.904
Yeah.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.239
And of course, sooner

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:14.974
would benefit the Ukrainians

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.610
because they are less numerous.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.045
And the Russians,

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.581
Putin thinks he can outwait the West

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.249
and obviously unity.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:25.318
And and all of this is being tested

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:26.552
right now.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.621
I want to ask you a couple of things

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.690
just to follow up on what you just said.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.559
If you were the commander,

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.528
what the battle

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.663
you know, the battle zone commander now,

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:41.567
what would you say Ukraine needs in order

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:44.404
to have a successful counter offensive?

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.105
What does it need to focus on

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:48.241
and what equipment, training?

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.443
You know, sophisticated armed systems

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.511
does it need now?

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:53.613
They've been

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.882
the Ukrainians have been exceptional

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.750
in training

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.152
throughout this fight

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:00.553
over the course of the last year.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.422
And actually before that.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:03.089
I would argue

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.490
that a great deal of the training

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.527
they did between Crimea in 2014

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:09.328
and 20, 22

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.930
has served them exceptionally well.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.932
They continue to train

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.567
and this combined arms training

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.836
I think that they are going through

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:19.172
now will make a significant difference

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:20.573
in the future fight

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.141
and that's what I would emphasize.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.210
And then back that up, obviously

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.211
with the weapons

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:27.079
and the systems that they need.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:30.082
Many people are chasing the the F-16.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:32.018
It's almost like it's a shiny object.

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.152
And I think eventually

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:36.122
we'll get two F-16s for the Ukrainians.

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:37.256
But in the meantime,

00:07:37.256 --> 00:07:38.958
that's not really what they need.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:39.826
They need

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:41.093
the kind of artillery,

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:41.894
more high margin,

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.530
more precision guided munitions

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.766
to be able to strike deep

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:47.600
at the Russians

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.701
and have the kind of impact

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.902
they've had in the past.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:51.070
That to me.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.773
Well, I think make a huge difference

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.575
in what happens over the course

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:57.577
of the next six or seven months.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.679
Look, let me push back a little bit.

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:02.582
You say in many, many in the in the NATO,

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:03.816
you know, group

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:06.085
says that that's not what they need

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.753
when they talk about fighter jets.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:09.222
But, you know,

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:11.324
the leopard tank was a shiny object

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.326
that was being held back for a long time.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:15.294
And now they are getting them

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:15.561
at least

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:15.928
they're trying

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.597
to get them as fast as they can.

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:18.764
And you all are saying that

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:19.565
actually they need

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:20.566
that kind of

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:23.636
of of projection of power, etc.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:24.670
So why do you think

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.772
they don't need aircraft?

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:28.341
And what we also have heard

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:29.041
is that some

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:31.077
Ukrainians are being trained outside,

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:32.311
including in the United States

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:34.313
on simulators to figure out,

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:36.682
you know, exactly how to furnish them

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:37.817
with these fighter jets,

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:38.951
whatever they might be.

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:40.953
Why do you think they don't need them?

00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:43.189
I don't

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.090
think I

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:44.991
didn't mean to say

00:08:44.991 --> 00:08:46.659
I don't think they don't need them.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:48.895
I think they will eventually get them.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:49.896
You mentioned

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:50.730
the training

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.299
that is being reported right now.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.367
What they really need

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:55.101
and they have actually been

00:08:55.101 --> 00:08:55.801
very good

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:56.435
at this is

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.971
they need the air defense systems

00:08:58.971 --> 00:08:59.605
And if you go back

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.140
to very early in the war,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.042
the number of Russian aircraft

00:09:03.042 --> 00:09:04.477
that got shot down

00:09:04.477 --> 00:09:06.245
in the first couple of months

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.980
was really extraordinary.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.416
So the the ability to impact,

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:13.586
you know, the Russian aircraft as well.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:14.887
And I recognize that

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:15.988
at some point in time,

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:17.223
we're going to have to go deeper

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.258
because there are Russian aircraft

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:21.060
launching weapons from inside Russia,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.162
which is where we don't want to go.

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:24.497
And I just think,

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:26.566
Christiane, that that it's going to take

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:28.534
it's going to take a little more time

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:30.469
to develop that capability

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:32.672
to get them to a point where those

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:35.107
where the F-16s would be

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:37.643
handled in an optimum way,

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:39.312
I think they're coming

00:09:39.312 --> 00:09:41.047
obviously not as fast as both

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:42.281
President Zelensky

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:43.749
and his military would like.

